{"title":"Career Roadmap · Subject Specialist","role":"Subject Specialist","summary":"A Subject Specialist is an education professional with strong expertise in a particular academic discipline combined with professional teacher-training and pedagogical skills.","facts":{"Current degree":"Other Teacher Education (D.El.Ed / B.El.Ed / B.P.Ed / ITEP / Integrated B.Sc-B.Ed / BA-B.Ed)","Course":"Integrated Teacher Education (ITEP / B.Sc-B.Ed / BA-B.Ed)"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Subject Specialist is an education professional with strong expertise in a particular academic discipline combined with professional teacher-training and pedagogical skills."},{"type":"p","text":"Depending on the integrated program and employment setting, the subject could be:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Physics"},{"text":"Chemistry"},{"text":"Biology"},{"text":"Mathematics"},{"text":"Computer Science"},{"text":"Geography"},{"text":"History"},{"text":"Political Science"},{"text":"Economics"},{"text":"English"},{"text":"Hindi"},{"text":"Regional languages"},{"text":"Commerce"},{"text":"Other school-level subjects"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The role can involve:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Teaching a specialized subject"},{"text":"Developing lesson plans"},{"text":"Designing assessments"},{"text":"Identifying learning gaps"},{"text":"Developing subject resources"},{"text":"Mentoring students"},{"text":"Supporting other teachers"},{"text":"Curriculum implementation"},{"text":"Academic coordination"},{"text":"Educational technology"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Qualification note","text":"“Subject Specialist” is a broad occupational title rather than one universally regulated job title. Eligibility depends on the subject, teaching level, recruiting organization and current recruitment rules. An ITEP/integrated B.Sc-B.Ed or BA-B.Ed provides an integrated subject + teacher-education pathway, but 